<title>USA: Florida citrus belt sees hot weather and rain-FASS.</title>
<headline>Florida citrus belt sees hot weather and rain-FASS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hot temperatures blanked the Florida citrus belt during the week ended June 22, but moisture remained adequate in most areas after several rainy days, the Florida Agricultural Statistics Service (FASS), said.</p>
<p>High temperatures averaged between 88 to 92 (degrees Fahrenheit), with lows mostly in the 70s. Rainfall reached a quarter of an inch to one-and-two-thirds inches.</p>
<p>New crop fruit continues to progress and fruit size remains normal, as the citrus harvest is nearly complete, FASS said.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
